@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #555555
}

actor Guest
actor Parent
actor Specialist
actor Admin

rectangle "SEN Support Platform" {
  usecase "SC-01\nRegister, sign in,\nview own account" as SC01
  usecase "SC-02\nCreate, view, edit\nchild profile" as SC02
  usecase "SC-03\nPlan, view, update,\nor cancel support session" as SC03
  usecase "SC-04\nCreate, read, edit,\ndelete diary entries" as SC04
  usecase "SC-05\nInspect diary entry\nversion history" as SC05
  usecase "SC-06\nView permitted\naudit events" as SC06
  usecase "SC-07\nManage accounts, guardians,\nand specialist assignments" as SC07
  usecase "SC-08\nExport permitted\nchild records" as SC08
  usecase "SC-09\nDelete child data" as SC09
}

' слева: Guest и Parent
Guest  --> SC01
Parent --> SC01
Parent --> SC02
Parent --> SC03
Parent --> SC04
Parent --> SC05
Parent --> SC06
Parent --> SC07
Parent --> SC08
Parent --> SC09

' справа: Specialist и Admin
SC01 <-- Specialist
SC02 <-- Specialist
SC03 <-- Specialist
SC04 <-- Specialist
SC05 <-- Specialist

SC01 <-- Admin
SC02 <-- Admin
SC06 <-- Admin
SC07 <-- Admin
SC08 <-- Admin
SC09 <-- Admin

legend bottom
  **Notes**
  SC-01: Guest is limited to public pages, registration and sign-in; no child data.
  SC-02: Only Parent creates a profile. Parent and Specialist need a valid child relationship. Only the primary guardian edits. Admin sees metadata only.
  SC-03: Within the actor's permissions and child relationship. Specialist updates or cancels assigned sessions only. Admin sees aggregates only (not a use case link).
  SC-04: Parent creates shared entries only and reads shared entries. Specialist also reads specialists-only entries. Edit and delete apply to own entries only. Specialist cannot delete (edits are versioned, AUD-03).
  SC-05: Only for diary entries the actor is authorized to read.
  SC-06: Parent sees access events for a related child. Admin also sees the system-wide log. No diary content.
  SC-07: Admin manages user accounts. Parent acts as primary guardian only: links guardians, creates and ends specialist assignments.
  SC-08: Parent (primary guardian) exports profile, sessions and shared diary entries. Admin exports metadata only, on documented request, audited.
  SC-09: Parent (primary guardian), or Admin on documented request, audited. Diary text is never displayed to Admin.
endlegend
@enduml